[h1]R.A.T.S. Topographic Map[/h1]
[i]R.A.T.S. – Reconnaissance, Acoustics, Terrain & Signals[/i]

[b]Stop flying blind over the terrain.[/b]
Land heights and sea depths on your tactical map: for low-level flying, terrain masking, radar horizons and room to dive.

[quote]▶ [b]Requires[/b] a mod loader: [b]R.A.T.S. Keel[/b] (Required items, top right) or Anchor Chain, either one
✉ Bugs, ideas, questions: [url=https://hub.sewerlabs.dev/s/topo]R.A.T.S. feedback board[/url]
⭐ A favourite helps other captains find it[/quote]

[h2]✦ New in 1.6[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]One menu button[/b] in the map's title bar: Topography, Look, Legend, Cursor height
[*][b]Runs on 0.9.1[/b] and the flat map (0.8.7)
[/list]

[h2]✦ Highlights[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Heights and depths at a glance.[/b] 13 height bands, 12 depth bands, hill shading, contour lines that follow your zoom
[*][b]Terrain that hits back.[/b] Select an aircraft: terrain at or above its altitude is hatched red, with the clearance
[*][b]Room to dive.[/b] Select a submarine: below the thermal layer, where the layer ends, where it gets too shallow
[*][b]19 looks, day and night.[/b] ECDIS, Soviet General Staff map, survey sonar, phosphor green, red light and more
[*][b]Your own look[/b] from a small text file; the map updates when you save
[*][b]Made for the 3D globe.[/b] Lined up at every zoom, at high latitudes, across the date line and over the poles
[*][b]Height under the pointer[/b] in metres and feet, in the mission editor too
[/list]

[h2]▶ Quick start[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe; Steam offers R.A.T.S. Keel with it if you have no mod loader
[*]Switch R.A.T.S. Topographic Map on in Mods
[*]Open the map in a mission: the layer is already on
[/olist]
[list]
[*][b]The menu:[/b] the mountain mark in the map's title bar, left of the map menu; in the editor at the top right of its map
[*][b]Keys:[/b] F6 on/off, Shift+F6 next look
[/list]

[h2]⚙ The looks[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Day:[/b] Standard, army tactical map, Soviet General Staff map, bathymetric chart, ECDIS (IHO S-52), desert storm, satellite, 1940s chart, glacier
[*][b]Night:[/b] Midnight, Standard, Black, recon photo, survey sonar, combat display, phosphor green, white phosphor, amber, red light
[*][b]Your own:[/b] Look, Save this look, edit the .ini; every key is in [url=https://github.com/struckl/SeaPowerTopo/blob/main/docs/themes.md]docs/themes.md[/url]
[/list]

[h2]⚠ Good to know[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]The game's own heights and depths,[/b] from its terrain data, with the height and depth factors from Options, World
[*][b]Display only.[/b] Units, missions and saves are untouched; symbols, waypoints and labels stay on top
[*][b]Drawn once at mission start,[/b] so nothing is redrawn while you play zoomed out
[*][b]Works with Better TacMap[/b]
[/list]

[h2]⚙ Settings[/h2]
[list]
[*][i]BepInEx\config\dev.sewerlabs.seapowertopo.cfg[/i], editable with the game open
[*][b]Map:[/b] keys, looks for day and night, opacity, hill shading, contours, band starts, sea tint, safety contour
[*][b]Units:[/b] red terrain for aircraft, thermal layer for submarines
[*][b]Readout:[/b] height under cursor, metres / feet / both, the Legend entry
[/list]

[h2]⚙ Install and game versions[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]R.A.T.S. Keel:[/b] https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3835527459
